  {"icon":"🗳️","site":"Both","title":"Meta ad prices are easing after Election Day, but the spend ramp is a few days late","when":"Nov 5","url":"https://grid-articore.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0C9X6MHV89/p1793806383964839","refs":[{"go":"tp|channel/Paid Social","l":"TeePublic Paid Social"},{"go":"rb|channel/Paid Social","l":"Redbubble Paid Social"}],"status":"Watching","tone":"open","channel":"#peak_daily_performance_standup","fx":"Partly: cheaper ads can bring more paid social visitors, which can lower CVR without a site problem.","body":"In the USA, Meta ad costs are down 6 to 8% day over day after the election, short of the 10 to 12% hoped for. Spend ramped a few days later than planned: Nov 5 shows stronger day-over-day gains on TeePublic, while Redbubble responds less because its spend is held back on purpose to protect profit. An hourly cost-per-order tracker now covers about 90% of media spend, with checks every 4 hours this weekend.","tldr":"Meta ads are 6 to 8% cheaper after the election and the spend ramp is a few days late, with TeePublic responding first.","pts":["USA only: 6 to 8% lower media cost day over day, against the 10 to 12% hoped for.","Nov 5 showed stronger day-over-day gains on TeePublic; Redbubble is less responsive.","Hourly cost-per-order checks run about every 4 hours this weekend."],"why":"If paid social sessions rise while CVR dips, cheaper ads are the first thing to check."},
  {"icon":"🔍","site":"RB","title":"Redbubble launched a bolder search bar for everyone on Nov 5, with no A/B test","when":"Nov 5","url":"https://grid-articore.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0V4PM9DW/p1793898060979829","refs":[{"go":"rb|overall","l":"Redbubble CVR"}],"status":"Live","tone":"good","channel":"#released","fx":"Partly: it went live on Nov 5, so only the last day shown is touched. There is no control group; the team will compare search use before and after.","body":"Redbubble's search box now has a fully rounded input, a bolder border, a larger red button and animated stars. Only 9% of Redbubble visitors use search against 20% on TeePublic, and searchers are tied to more orders, so the aim is more search use ahead of peak. It went to everyone, so the read is before and after, keeping peak seasonality in mind.","tldr":"Redbubble's more prominent search bar is live for everyone, and the team will compare search use before and after.","pts":["Only 9% of Redbubble visitors use search, against 20% on TeePublic.","Searchers are tied to more orders, which is the case for making search easier to see.","It is not an A/B test, so peak seasonality has to be kept in mind when reading it."],"qs":["How do the visitors who never search find designs?"],"why":"If Redbubble search use rises from Nov 5 but CVR does not, check the sale and traffic mix before crediting the search bar."},
  {"icon":"🏷️","site":"TP","title":"TeePublic raises sale prices on long sleeves, UK classic tees, totes, pins and hats from Nov 6","when":"Nov 5","url":"https://grid-articore.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0V4PM9DW/p1793930000821919","refs":[{"go":"tp|overall","l":"TeePublic CVR"}],"status":"Live Nov 6","tone":"warn","channel":"#released","fx":"No: the changes start Nov 6 (US time), so none of the numbers shown include them. Small price rises can trim CVR on those products.","body":"Sale prices only change from Nov 6 (US time): UK classic tee up 2 pounds to 15, USA long sleeve tees up $1, USA totes up $1 (not the new canvas tote), USA pins up 25 cents and USA dad and baseball hats up $1 each. USA kids hoodie goes down $1 to try to win back share of a higher-profit product. The aim is gross profit through peak.","tldr":"TeePublic nudges sale prices up on several products from Nov 6, and cuts the kids hoodie by $1.","pts":["UK classic tee up 2 pounds, to 15 pounds.","USA long sleeve tees, totes and hats up $1; pins up 25 cents.","USA kids hoodie down $1 to rebuild share of a higher-profit product."],"why":"If CVR or average order value moves on Nov 6 or later, check these sale price changes before looking for a site issue."},
  {"icon":"🧥","site":"Both","title":"Pushing higher-profit products would add profit dollars but lower the margin percent","when":"Nov 4","url":"https://grid-articore.enterprise.slack.com/archives/C0C9X6MHV89/p1793825995911849","refs":[],"status":"Open","tone":"open","channel":"#peak_daily_performance_standup","fx":"No: nothing has changed on the site. It is a question about what the email feed and search results should push.","body":"With cold weather arriving, the group asked whether leaning into fleece would lift gross profit dollars. T-shirts carry the higher margin percent on both brands (TeePublic 52.1% vs 45.7% for fleece over 28 days, Redbubble 55.0% vs 49.0%), while fleece earns more profit dollars per unit ($17.00 vs $10.77). More fleece would lower the overall percent, so it depends which target matters. The email feed would need extra feeds to carry it, and the group agreed it is worth testing, including in search results.","tldr":"Fleece earns more profit dollars per unit but lowers the margin percent; the group wants to test it.","pts":["T-shirts have the higher margin percent on both brands.","Fleece earns $17.00 per unit against $10.77 for T-shirts.","The email feed would need additional feeds to promote it."],"qs":["Which matters more through peak: profit dollars or margin percent?"],"why":"If average order value or margin percent shifts in search or email, check whether the product mix changed."}
