  {"date":"2026-11-05","tldr":"Revenue was a little below the prior day as the paid spend ramp ran late, with TeePublic stronger on Nov 5. The group plans to cut the stackable sign-up offer from 25% to 10% to protect gross profit, with a decision by Monday.","items":[{"icon":"📈","site":"Both","title":"Nov 4 revenue slightly lower on both sites as spend ramps late","refs":[{"go":"tp|overall","l":"TeePublic CVR"},{"go":"rb|overall","l":"Redbubble CVR"}],"status":"Nov 4 read","tone":"done","impact":"Both sites a little lower day over day; Nov 5 stronger on TeePublic","owner":"Commercial","detail":"Revenue (MPR) on Nov 4 was below plan and last year, with both sites slightly lower than Nov 3. Paid spend ramped a few days later than planned, and Nov 5 shows stronger day-over-day gains on TeePublic while Redbubble responds less. The group is checking whether the daily plan shape matches the real ramp. Last year spend was too soft going into Black Friday, so this year's plan models more growth into Black Friday and Cyber Monday.","watch":"tp|overall","watchLabel":"TeePublic CVR"},{"icon":"🎟️","site":"TP","title":"Stackable sign-up offer: cut from 25% to 10%","nx":"Assess and prioritize by Monday Nov 9","status":"Planned","tone":"soon","impact":"Saves an estimated 45 to 70 basis points of discount","owner":"Product","detail":"Product builds it and Marketing updates the creative for every use of the offer. The target is the sprint starting next week. Longer term the team needs an A/B testing framework to compare 15, 20 and 25% offers."},{"icon":"🏷️","site":"TP","title":"Sale prices up on long sleeves, UK classic tees and totes from Nov 6","status":"Live Nov 6","tone":"soon","impact":"More gross profit per order; small CVR risk on those products","owner":"Pricing","detail":"USA long sleeve tees are up $1 to $2 (their share is up 2% on last year), the UK classic tee is up 2 pounds (80% of UK orders, discount rate 38%, still $1 below Redbubble), and USA totes are a low-dollar, lower-priority change."},{"icon":"🧥","site":"TP","title":"Heavyweight tee upsell: release targeted next week","nx":"Put it at the top of the Customer team's sprint list","status":"Building","tone":"soon","impact":"Adds revenue and gross profit dollars, but not the margin percent","owner":"Customer team","detail":"The Customer team is building the upsell now and aims to release it next week. It helps dollars rather than the gross profit percent, so it should not be expected to move that number."},{"icon":"📦","site":"TP","title":"Peak shipping surcharge built, kept on a switch","status":"Ready","tone":"soon","impact":"A 40 cent per-order charge, off unless needed","owner":"PLC team","detail":"The Purchase Lifecycle team is building a 40 cent per-order peak shipping charge behind a feature flag. It will not be turned on unless needed, but it lets the company act fast."},{"icon":"⏱️","site":"Both","title":"Hourly cost-per-order tracker and weekend coverage","nx":"Share the tracker and set checks about every 4 hours this weekend","status":"Planned","tone":"soon","impact":"TeePublic roughly on target; Redbubble intentionally under","owner":"Paid media","detail":"A sheet tracks hourly paid spend against revenue for both sites, covering about 90% of media spend. Checks run about every 4 hours this weekend with the India team adding coverage, aiming for near 24-hour coverage as peak approaches. Checkout timers on TeePublic are being scheduled for the end of next week, leaning Nov 13 (last year Nov 19)."}],"next":[["Product","Assess and prioritize the 25% to 10% sign-up offer cut by Monday Nov 9"],["Customer team","Move the heavyweight tee upsell to the top of the sprint, release next week"],["Paid media","Share the hourly cost-per-order tracker and set weekend checks about every 4 hours"],["Operations","Settle the TeePublic checkout timer go-live date, leaning Nov 13"]]},
  {"date":"2026-11-04","tldr":"TeePublic had a very strong Nov 3, while Redbubble is running well behind plan and last year. Gross profit is about 2 points behind plan because of discounts, so the group is weighing a smaller new-account coupon or a minimum order and a look at UK pricing, with options due at tomorrow's standup. Meta ad prices are easing after Election Day.","items":[{"icon":"📈","site":"Both","title":"TeePublic well ahead on Nov 3; Redbubble behind","refs":[{"go":"tp|overall","l":"TeePublic CVR"},{"go":"rb|overall","l":"Redbubble CVR"}],"status":"Nov 3 read","tone":"done","impact":"TeePublic far above plan and last year; Redbubble running well below","owner":"Commercial","detail":"TeePublic MPR on Nov 3 was far above plan and last year, on 9,646 orders at an average order value of $39.55, helped by the election (last year was not an election year) and a promotion that is compared against last year. Redbubble was the weaker site: Nov 3 was down 17% on last year and Nov 4 was running about 24% below plan and 30% below last year. A countdown timer reset is expected to push Redbubble CPR up slightly today.","watch":"rb|overall","watchLabel":"Redbubble CVR"},{"icon":"🏷️","site":"Both","title":"Gross profit gap: undiscounted product margin about 2 points below plan","nx":"Come back with options at tomorrow's standup","status":"Deciding","tone":"open","impact":"Two levers: the stackable new-account coupon and international pricing","owner":"Pricing","detail":"Undiscounted product margin is about 200 basis points below plan, a known pre-peak variable. Two ways to close it were discussed: cut the stackable new-account coupon, or adjust international pricing and discounts, mostly the UK. TeePublic's discount rate is also inflated because non-sale classic tee prices were raised to $24 this year. There is no way to A/B test these changes, so decisions are directional."},{"icon":"🎟️","site":"TP","title":"New-account coupon: cut from 25% to 10%, or add a minimum order","nx":"Check whether a minimum order of about $40 works and whether the cut adds gross profit","status":"Deciding","tone":"open","impact":"About 45 basis points of discount if use holds; used on 3% of orders","owner":"Product","detail":"The stackable coupon is used on 3% of orders (first and second purchases). Cutting it to 10% saves about 45 basis points if the take rate holds, but fewer orders could cancel that. A minimum order was suggested instead: 44% of orders over the last 3 days were $39 or less, so a threshold would keep the take rate while lifting profit dollars. It is technically possible; two codes live at once is a product constraint, and emails already went out with the 25% offer."},{"icon":"🌍","site":"Both","title":"UK and international pricing and discounts under review","nx":"Review UK overlap data and align on international options before the next standup","status":"Review","tone":"open","impact":"International margin is lower than the USA","owner":"Pricing","detail":"TeePublic may be taking Redbubble orders internationally, especially in the UK, since the feed changes. Localized pricing is possible for the top five currencies on TeePublic. International growth came from removing international shipping charges, not discounts, so pulling back international marketing would slow TeePublic growth. A low-risk trial of a higher promo price on one UK product was discussed."},{"icon":"🗳️","site":"Both","title":"Meta ad prices easing after Election Day","nx":"Watch whether the drop deepens over the next few days","status":"Watching","tone":"open","impact":"USA ad costs down 6 to 8% day over day","owner":"Paid media","detail":"USA Meta ad costs fell 6 to 8% after the election, short of the 10 to 12% hoped for given how much rates rose this year. Some lag is possible, so the drop may deepen."},{"icon":"🛒","site":"RB","title":"Redbubble Shopping shows no return-on-ad-spend growth yet","nx":"Look for small tweaks, especially the recently added products","status":"Planned","tone":"soon","impact":"Redbubble Shopping spend not yet scaling","owner":"Paid media","detail":"There is no growth in return on ad spend on Redbubble Shopping yet. Marketing will review small tweaks, especially for the recently added seasonal products, to find more demand."}],"next":[["Product","Check if a minimum order of about $40 works for the new-account coupon and whether cutting it adds gross profit"],["Pricing","Review UK overlap data and international discount options"],["Paid media","Review Redbubble Shopping for small tweaks on recently added products"]]},
  {"date":"2026-11-03","tldr":"Nov 2 was a strong sale day, with both brands together close to last year. Discount rates on sticker bundles and coupons are running higher than planned, the new device split on A/B tests shows desktop and mobile moving in opposite directions, and ad costs should ease after Election Day.","items":[{"icon":"📈","site":"Both","title":"Strong sale day on Nov 2","refs":[{"go":"tp|overall","l":"TeePublic CVR"}],"status":"Nov 2 read","tone":"done","impact":"Well above a normal non-sale day; both brands close to last year","owner":"Commercial","detail":"Orders were far above the last non-sale day under the 40% TeePublic sale, and TeePublic and Redbubble together landed close to last year, which is a good sign this early in the season. Product margin and shipping margin were both up on last year.","watch":"tp|overall","watchLabel":"TeePublic CVR"},{"icon":"🏷️","site":"Both","title":"Discount rate is running above plan","nx":"Treat the extra discount as a known cost through peak and size other levers around it","status":"Watching","tone":"open","impact":"Coupons and the 50% off 10+ sticker bundles are the main drivers","owner":"Finance","detail":"Both brands are giving more discount than planned, mostly through email coupons and the 10+ sticker bundles. The group agreed not to cut coupons just to hit a percentage, and to optimize for profit dollars instead. The TeePublic sale runs through Nov 8."},{"icon":"🧮","site":"Both","title":"Sticker bundle discounts under review","nx":"Review the bundle structure with the category manager and test discounts at 4 to 7 stickers","status":"Next week","tone":"soon","impact":"Going from 8 or 9 stickers to 10 added little or nothing","owner":"Pricing","detail":"The 50% off 10+ bundle was retested after a double-digit drop in those orders, but moving shoppers from 8 or 9 stickers up to 10 adds flat or negative value. Large stickers in bundles also put pressure on shipping margin on both brands. Automated price testing starts with 10+ stickers, with write-ups expected next week."},{"icon":"📱","site":"Both","title":"A/B tests split by device show opposite results","status":"New read","tone":"open","impact":"Cart cross-sell and style pills help on mobile, not desktop","owner":"Product","detail":"With results split by desktop and mobile, the cart cross-sell and the T-shirt style pills both lower revenue per user on desktop and raise it on mobile. The best seller badge helps, mostly on mobile. TeePublic tests cannot be split by device yet."},{"icon":"🔍","site":"TP","title":"Organic search CVR dip flagged","refs":[{"go":"tp|channel/Organic Search","l":"TeePublic Organic Search"}],"nx":"Read the explanation already posted in Slack","status":"Open","tone":"open","impact":"Explanation posted, not yet reviewed","owner":"Commercial","detail":"Organic search CVR was flagged as down, and an explanation was posted in Slack after the call. It is still to be reviewed before deciding whether anything needs fixing."},{"icon":"🗳️","site":"Both","title":"Meta ad prices rose on Election Day","nx":"Check ad prices Thursday and Friday and push spend if they ease","status":"Planned","tone":"soon","impact":"Relief expected Thursday through Saturday","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Meta ad prices rose another 8.5% in the USA today. Marketing expects relief from Thursday to Saturday as election spending clears, and plans to push spend then and test the lift. On Redbubble, about 30% of one product volume has moved to a lower-cost fulfiller, with savings expected today."},{"icon":"📄","site":"Both","title":"Paper products need their own pricing","nx":"Set up a dedicated pricing conversation before next year","status":"Open","tone":"open","impact":"Current discount and shipping logic is built around apparel","owner":"Pricing","detail":"Stationery, notebooks, greeting cards and posters do not fit tools built for apparel. Volume discounts, per-unit price display and stackability rules all need rethinking. TeePublic is testing a 10% discount on notebooks, wall art, greeting cards, acrylic blocks and totes so the 15% bundle message stays visible, and more analyst help arrives Monday to speed up price testing."}],"next":[["Commercial","Review the explanation for the organic search CVR dip"],["Finance","Plan around the discount rate running above plan through peak"],["Pricing","Review the 10+ sticker bundle discount with the category manager and the promotions team"],["Paid media","Check Meta ad prices Thursday and Friday and push spend if they ease"],["Pricing","Align on stationery and paper product pricing"]]},
  {"date":"2026-11-02","tldr":"Both sites converted solidly on Nov 1 against recent comparable days. Redbubble is still running behind plan on organic traffic and paid social conversion, and the team is waiting on the post-election drop in ad costs before leaning in on paid social.","items":[{"icon":"📈","site":"TP","title":"Conversion solid, and year-over-year is now in the tracker","refs":[{"go":"tp|overall","l":"TeePublic CVR"}],"status":"Nov 1 read","tone":"done","impact":"Above recent comparable days and above last year","owner":"Commercial","detail":"TeePublic is comping well against last year and its CVR held up on the first day of the sale. The tracker now shows a day-and-date year-over-year view for TeePublic, and both measures sit above their baselines. Paid social CVR is improving against other channels after the spend cut and a better Meta feed, while organic search still lags.","watch":"tp|overall","watchLabel":"TeePublic CVR"},{"icon":"📉","site":"RB","title":"Redbubble is still behind plan, with a steady gap since mid-October","refs":[{"go":"rb|overall","l":"Redbubble CVR"}],"nx":"Keep watching organic product page traffic after the consolidation","status":"Watching","tone":"open","impact":"Gap has barely moved since about Oct 18","owner":"Commercial","detail":"Redbubble CVR was solid against recent comparable days, but the sales gap to plan has stayed steady since the paid optimization began about Oct 18. Search results traffic has stabilized, while product page traffic is declining faster after the consolidation. A 50% sale in Australia that started Nov 1 explains the spike in the discount rate."},{"icon":"📌","site":"RB","title":"Paid social and organic CVR down about a third versus other channels","refs":[{"go":"rb|channel/Paid Social","l":"Redbubble Paid Social"}],"nx":"Check whether the Pinterest mix explains it","status":"Likely mix","tone":"open","impact":"Looks like more Pinterest traffic, not more spend","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Paid social CVR on Redbubble fell about 33% and organic about 31% against other channels. The team thinks it is the Pinterest traffic mix rather than a spend increase. Pinterest clicks are very cheap, which makes up for their lower conversion."},{"icon":"🚚","site":"TP","title":"TeePublic shipping price increases are paying off","nx":"Check whether the increases are holding back conversion","status":"Analyzing","tone":"open","impact":"Shipping margin well above plan; conversion effect unknown","owner":"Pricing","detail":"Shipping margin on TeePublic was far above plan on Nov 1. The open question is whether the higher shipping prices are suppressing CVR. Margin on undiscounted products ran slightly below plan, and a large product volume moved to a lower-cost fulfiller today, with the effect expected tomorrow."},{"icon":"🗳️","site":"Both","title":"Waiting on cheaper ads after the Nov 4 election","nx":"Hold budgeted cost per order through Friday, then reassess","status":"Planned","tone":"soon","impact":"Paid social could get a lift if CVR holds","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Marketing expects Meta ad prices on TeePublic, which is mostly US traffic, to ease for about a week after the election, before holiday spending competes. Redbubble paid search and shopping ran a little conservative today, and its email and text sends are held until intent picks up Thursday and Friday. An hourly cost-per-order chart for Google and Meta is the guardrail for peak."},{"icon":"🧭","site":"Both","title":"Marketing test scoreboard and a new standup format","nx":"Build the tracker and start the split format Nov 17","status":"This week","tone":"soon","impact":"One place to see marketing test wins and losses","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Marketing will build a wins-and-losses tracker for image, expansion and Google tests in a shared sheet this week. From Nov 17 the operational items, such as shipping cutoffs and customer service tickets, move to a separate meeting, and this call stays on financial results, triage and deep dives."}],"next":[["Commercial","Decide how to include shipping margin in the daily tracker"],["Paid media","Build the marketing test wins-and-losses tracker"],["Paid media","Finish the hourly cost-per-order chart for Google and Meta"],["Paid media","Compare US and non-US performance to size the post-election lift"],["Commercial","Find out what drove the Redbubble discount rate spike"]]},
  {"date":"2026-10-30","tldr":"Oct 29 was a strong day, led by TeePublic's Brewers surge. Hold current discounts and price changes for about a week before adjusting, and watch the style pills and topics navigation tests on Redbubble.","items":[{"icon":"📈","site":"TP","title":"Strong day, led by Brewers demand","refs":[{"go":"tp|overall","l":"TeePublic CVR"}],"status":"Oct 29 read","tone":"done","impact":"Up about 30% on last year; about 10% without Wisconsin","owner":"Commercial","detail":"TeePublic was well above last year on Oct 29, with about two-thirds of the growth coming from Wisconsin during the Brewers run. Without Wisconsin it was still up around 10%. Brewers content should fade through the weekend, and last year's World Series gave no tough comparison for Nov 1.","watch":"tp|overall","watchLabel":"TeePublic CVR"},{"icon":"🧮","site":"Both","title":"Margin pressure from discounts and shipping","nx":"Hold discounts and price changes for a week before adjusting","status":"Holding","tone":"open","impact":"Too many changes in flight to read the signal yet","owner":"Pricing","detail":"Margin ran a little below plan because of the active coupon and the shipping price increases. All TeePublic product price changes finish today, Redbubble shipping changes are already live, and a new fulfiller is finishing onboarding this week. The group agreed to leave discounts and prices alone for at least a week rather than pull back marketing."},{"icon":"👕","site":"RB","title":"Style pills test on product pages","nx":"Fix the order value calculation, then likely roll out","status":"Live since Oct 27","tone":"soon","impact":"Revenue per session up about 2% in the test group","owner":"Customer team","detail":"Shoppers in the test group add to cart a little less often but spend more per order, which lifts revenue per session. The order value metric is miscalculated and needs a fix before the team confirms gross profit per visitor. Mobile versus desktop tagging on Redbubble is broken in Amplitude, with a fix targeted next week."},{"icon":"🧭","site":"RB","title":"Topics-first navigation test","nx":"Align on continuing the test","status":"Keep running","tone":"open","impact":"Engagement is up, CVR change is not significant","owner":"Customer team","detail":"Engagement is significantly higher and CVR is down but not significantly. The group leans toward continuing on Redbubble because the engagement signal improves retargeting. Open question is whether leading with T-shirts lifts order value enough to offset any margin drag. The stickers cross-sell launched Oct 29 and needs more time to read."},{"icon":"📣","site":"RB","title":"Long sleeves in the feed, more products next week","refs":[{"go":"rb|channel/Paid Search (cpc)","l":"Redbubble Paid Search"}],"nx":"Confirm whether a higher-quality image feed can be built","status":"Scaling this weekend","tone":"soon","impact":"More products competing in paid ads","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Long-sleeve shirts are now in the Redbubble feed and spend scales this weekend. Eight new product categories join the feed next week with a gradual ramp. A higher-quality image test needs a secondary feed, and paid media is checking whether it can be built."},{"icon":"🛠️","site":"Both","title":"Data tooling and access","nx":"Fix access for the people still locked out","status":"In progress","tone":"open","impact":"One daily performance summary instead of conflicting ones","owner":"Data","detail":"A daily performance post to Slack is in testing and will replace manual summaries so numbers do not conflict. The LLM data tool is now connected to Slack, with Redbubble destination data still missing. Access for several attendees is being fixed."}],"next":[["Customer team","Send an async update on the pills and topics navigation tests"],["Paid media","Confirm if a higher-quality image feed is feasible"],["Product","Pair with paid media on an A/B test tracker for ads"],["Customer team","Align on continuing the topics navigation test on Redbubble"],["Data","Fix tool access for the people still locked out"]]},
  {"date":"2026-10-29","tldr":"Regional recommendations lifted CVR in email tests, so the team will explore state-level trending in navigation before the holidays. Redbubble abandoned cart events are now flowing.","items":[{"icon":"🌎","site":"TP","title":"Regional trending as a CVR lever","nx":"Review short-term ideas beyond email","status":"Promising","tone":"soon","impact":"State-level picks lifted CVR from about 1.8% to 2.8% in email","owner":"Customer team","detail":"International traffic is growing faster than US traffic, so a US-heavy feed gets less relevant. State-level recommendations lifted email CVR by about a full point, with lower order value but as a second purchase. The idea is to extend regional picks to SMS, navigation and other surfaces."},{"icon":"🧊","site":"RB","title":"New items struggle to get seen on Redbubble","nx":"Scope a reserved feed share for new items","status":"Proposed","tone":"open","impact":"New designs need a way into the feed","owner":"Product","detail":"The Redbubble feed rewards items that already get clicks, so a new item has no way to start. TeePublic has a cold start discount; Redbubble has nothing. Proposal: reserve a small feed share for new items, and let those with traction move into the main allocation after a trial."},{"icon":"🛒","site":"RB","title":"Abandoned cart events now flowing","nx":"Watch for impact data","status":"Started Oct 28","tone":"soon","impact":"Expected to be high impact","owner":"Marketing","detail":"Redbubble abandoned cart events, missing for years, started coming through yesterday. So far it is volume only with no results yet. Regional recommendations and abandoned cart recovery may stack."},{"icon":"🧭","site":"RB","title":"Rotating trending topics in navigation by state","nx":"Set up a working session Monday","status":"Exploring","tone":"open","impact":"Could ship before the holidays","owner":"Customer team","detail":"An engineer on the Customer team believes rotating trending topics in navigation by state, driven by an automatic algorithm, is feasible. The team will dig in together before the holidays."}],"next":[["Product","Set up a Monday session on state-level navigation trending"],["Product","Review short-term regional recommendation ideas"],["Search","Connect the search lead with the regional signal findings"]]},
  {"date":"2026-10-22","tldr":"Redbubble's 40% sale is not lifting orders the way it was planned, so watch Redbubble CVR while the team checks why pricier oversized tees show first in search and weighs a deeper classic tee discount. TeePublic's sale is on track through Sunday.","items":[{"icon":"📉","site":"RB","title":"Redbubble sale response is soft","refs":[{"go":"rb|overall","l":"Redbubble CVR"}],"nx":"Find out why the sale is not lifting CVR before peak promos start","status":"Day 2 of the sale","tone":"open","impact":"Peak is mostly sale days, so this matters most","owner":"Commercial","detail":"The Redbubble sale (up to 40% off) started Oct 21 and did not bring the lift the team expected. The gap between sale and non-sale prices is smaller on Redbubble than on TeePublic, and the recent base price increase lands at the same time.","watch":"rb|overall","watchLabel":"Redbubble CVR"},{"icon":"👕","site":"RB","title":"Search shows oversized and extra soft tees before classic","nx":"Trace why, and fix before peak if it is safe","status":"Investigating","tone":"soon","impact":"Classic tees are the cheapest option on sale","owner":"Product","detail":"On Redbubble search and browse pages, many T-shirts open on the oversized or extra soft style, which stay above $20 on sale while the classic tee is about $17. Search picks the best-selling version of each design, not the lowest-priced one. Artists can set a default color but not a default style."},{"icon":"🏷️","site":"RB","title":"Test a deeper discount on classic tees","nx":"Model the margin risk and break-even, then decide","status":"Deciding","tone":"open","impact":"Would bring classic tees to about $16, in line with TeePublic","owner":"Pricing","detail":"Idea: deepen the discount on Redbubble classic tees only, for the rest of this sale, to see how shoppers respond before peak. First step is working out how many extra orders it would take to pay for the lower price. Finance signs off on the risk."},{"icon":"🚚","site":"Both","title":"Shipping price changes","nx":"Start the TeePublic test as soon as possible","status":"Testing soon","tone":"soon","impact":"Better shipping margin through peak","owner":"Pricing","detail":"TeePublic will test $1 more shipping on orders with 2 or more T-shirts. Redbubble is raising shipping on orders where shipping was losing money. Shoppers were less sensitive to shipping prices during last year's peak."},{"icon":"🎟️","site":"RB","title":"Small sticker bundle discount trimmed","status":"Changing now","tone":"done","impact":"Stops losing money on 1 to 3 sticker orders","owner":"Pricing","detail":"The bundle discount for 1 to 3 stickers drops from 25% to 20%, because the deeper discount was losing money."},{"icon":"📣","site":"Both","title":"Ad spend adjusted after day 1","refs":[{"go":"tp|channel/Paid Search","l":"TeePublic Paid Search"}],"status":"Done Oct 22","tone":"done","impact":"Spend follows where sales are working","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Redbubble spend was pulled back after the sale did not lift as expected. TeePublic spend was nudged up because ad efficiency was strong, with a careful extra push on Google Shopping.","watch":"tp|channel/Paid Search","watchLabel":"TeePublic Paid Search"},{"icon":"⏱️","site":"Both","title":"Hourly ad spend vs revenue report","nx":"Share with the standup group","status":"Due Mon Oct 26","tone":"soon","impact":"Lets the team adjust spend within a sale day","owner":"Paid media","detail":"Meta and Google spend matched to hourly revenue, so the team can react during holiday sale days instead of waiting for the next day."},{"icon":"🛠️","site":"TP","title":"Short site outage this afternoon","status":"Back up","tone":"done","impact":"About 13 minutes of downtime","owner":"Engineering","detail":"The site was down for about 13 minutes shortly before standup on Oct 22 and is back up. The cause is still being confirmed. Expect a small dip in Oct 22 sessions and orders.","watch":"tp|sessions","watchLabel":"TeePublic sessions"}],"next":[["Product","Find why Redbubble search shows oversized and extra soft tees before classic"],["Pricing","Talk with pricing about a classic tee discount test on Redbubble"],["Finance","Sign off on the margin risk of that test"],["Pricing","Start the TeePublic shipping test on 2+ T-shirt orders"],["Paid media","Share the hourly spend vs revenue report by Mon Oct 26"]]}
